    "https://ecokedu.bamboohr.com/careers/157": {
      "title": "Education Coordinator",
      "description": "Education Coordinator. Department: College of Education and Psych. Full-Time. FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Position Summary The Education Coordinator is responsible for coordinating special projects within the Education department, focusing on revenue generation through scholarship programs and micro-credential programming, while providing administrative support and data analytics to drive enrollment and student success. The position also manages and helps advise students in secondary and alternative certification programs. Essential Job Duties • Coordinate activities and maintain records for the Inspired to Teach Incentive Program through Oklahoma State Regents for Higher Education (OSRHE), including semester degree verification checks for all applicants (200+ per semester). • Coordinate and support additional programs developed by OSRHE and the Oklahoma State Department of Education (OSDE) that assist alternative certification, traditional, and other teacher pathway candidates. • Coordinate and support ad hoc legislature driven state education scholarships, such as the Grow Your Own Educator Program initiative, etc. • Serve as academic advisor of record for approximately 53 graduate, non-degree-seeking students enrolled across five distinct alternative pathways to teacher certification, including individualized plan development and ongoing advisement through program completion. • Monitor Oklahoma teacher certification legislation and OSDE policy and guidance, including changes arising from state-level leadership transitions, and apply resulting changes accurately across all five alternative certification pathways. • Assist and advise secondary education majors with program advisement. • Maintain and develop micro-credential programs. • Provide administrative support and data analytics for department initiatives. • Plan and implement new processes, procedures, and projects. • Respond to queries and correspondence from students, employees, and the public. • Maintain and organize academic documents, files, and records. • Participate in departmental committees, including Assessment and Accreditation. • Host workshops and meetings for various educational programs, including workshops for secondary students and alternative certification candidates. • Build and maintain partnerships with Local Education Agencies (LEAs). • Coordinate the certification process and recommendations for certification. • Build and maintain partnerships with the Oklahoma State Department of Education (OSDE) Certification Unit. • Other duties as assigned by Supervisor or designee. Omission of specific statement of duties does not exclude them from the position if the work is similar, related or a logical assignment to the position. Qualifications • Bachelor's degree with 3-5 years of related experience. • Master's degree preferred. Licenses/Certifications • None Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Strong project management skills with ability to coordinate multiple initiatives simultaneously. • Proficient in providing administrative support and maintaining detailed records. • Demonstrated ability to build and maintain relationships with various stakeholders. • Strong analytical skills with ability to gather and analyze data for reporting purposes. • Excellent communication skills with ability to conduct workshops and presentations. • Knowledge of educational programs and certification processes. • Knowledge of grant writing and management practices. • Ability to track and interpret changes in Oklahoma teacher certification legislation and OSDE policy, and apply them across multiple certification pathways. • Ability to work independently and as part of a team. • Must have a strong work ethic and lead by example. • Must be a professional, credible and respected representative of the institution internally and in the community. • Demonstrated willingness and ability to act ethically and socially responsible. • Ability to communicate in a courteous manner. Physical Demands • Constantly required to remain in a seated position for extended periods • Frequently required to communicate effectively with diverse populations • Regularly performs tasks that involve repetitive wrist and finger movement • Regularly operates a computer and other standard office equipment • Occasionally required to move about the office and similar spaces Work Environment • The work is performed in a typical office setting with moderate noise levels from conversations and standard office equipment. • Some in-state and occasional out-of-state travel required. Supervisory Responsibility • None East Central University, in compliance with all applicable Federal and State laws and regulations, does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, age, religion, disability, marital status, genetic information, or status as a veteran in any of its policies, practices, or procedures. This includes but is not limited to admission, employment, financial aid, and educational services. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Employment Services Director, 1100 E. 14th St., Danley Hall 111, Ada, OK 74820, (580) 559-5260. Please ensure you have completed the Equal Opportunity Data Form with your application. https://www.ecok.edu/employment-services/equal_opportunity_data_form_accessible.pdf"
    },
    "https://ecokedu.bamboohr.com/careers/158": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant. Department: International Student Services. Full-Time. FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Grade: 6 Position Summary The Administrative Assistant is responsible for providing comprehensive administrative support to senior leadership through efficient management of schedules, communications, and office operations while ensuring organizational effectiveness and productivity. The International Students and Programs Administrative Assistant will assist the Director in managing international students from application to enrollment through graduation and post-graduation activities (Optimal Practical Training and the OPT-STEM extensions). • Provide administrative support to the leadership and department staff. • Manage day-to-day office operations to maintain an efficient and welcoming environment. • Serve as the front line of communications, including greeting visitors, handling incoming communications and addressing or redirecting properly. • Process requisitions and/or invoices for department expenditures. • Maintain physical and digital records through organized filing systems. • Assist with planning and coordination of university events. • Maintain office organization and supplies. • Provides advice regarding admissions policies and procedures including application due dates, and admissions criteria, the status of applications, admission decisions, required documentation, and other essential admissions information. • Assist former students with questions on Optimal Practical Training eligibility, applications, reporting, and deadlines. • Work with SEVIS and ICE. • Maintains and organizes files for the office. • Answer phone calls, emails and walk-ins. • Other duties as assigned by Supervisor or designee. Omission of specific statement of duties does not exclude them from the position if the work is similar, related or a logical assignment to the position. Qualifications • Minimum of 1-year experience in secretarial and/or office management and a high school diploma. • Experience in an administrative assistant position. Writing skills, verbal communication skills, and computer skills must be above entry-level. • Excellent interpersonal skills, including the ability to relate well to and work with individuals from diverse cultural backgrounds; demonstrated understanding of issues affecting international students. Licenses/Certifications • Valid driver's license Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Demonstrated ability to maintain strict confidentiality and handle sensitive information with professionalism • Strong organizational and time management skills with ability to manage multiple priorities • Excellent verbal and written communication skills with ability to interact professionally with diverse groups • Proficient in problem-solving and conflict resolution • Advanced knowledge of office technology and computer applications • Proven ability to work independently and exercise sound judgment • Strong project management skills with attention to detail • Must have a strong work ethic and lead by example • Must be a professional, credible and respected representative of the institution internally and in the community • Demonstrated willingness and ability to act ethically and socially responsible • Ability to communicate in a courteous manner Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of the job. Constantly required to remain in a seated position for extended periods Frequently required to communicate effectively with diverse populations Regularly performs tasks that involve repetitive wrist and finger movement Regularly operates a computer and other standard office equipment Occasionally required to move about the office and similar spaces Occasionally required to move objects weighing up to 10 pounds Work Environment The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The work is performed in a typical office setting with moderate noise levels from conversations, and standard office equipment. Supervisory Responsibility None East Central University, in compliance with all applicable Federal and State laws and regulations, does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, age, religion, disability, marital status, genetic information, or status as a veteran in any of its policies, practices, or procedures. This includes but is not limited to admission, employment, financial aid, and educational services. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Employment Services Director, 1100 E. 14th St., Danley Hall 111, Ada, OK 74820, (580) 559-5260. Please ensure you have completed the Equal Opportunity Data Form with your application. https://www.ecok.edu/employment-services/equal_opportunity_data_form_accessible.pdf"
